Module wrongboat "The Wrong Boat" {
  // ── Chapters, aims, and the ways it can end ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Chapter ch_quay "The Wrong Boat" when true "Two barges that look alike, a quay full of shouting, a mist that is lifting. Somebody is about to hand you something.".
  Chapter ch_afloat "Afloat" when since(9) and been(party, deck) "The Mary goes down the Aldwater at a walking pace, with onions, with a song, with the quay getting smaller and a thing in your pack that you cannot put down.".
  Chapter ch_fen "The Fen" when been(party, fen_landing) "Reeds, mist, one road, and every sound is a long way off or right beside you.".
  Chapter ch_fair "Pelham on Fair-day" when been(party, fairground) "A great many people, no one of whom is looking for you, and one of whom is.".
  Chapter ch_mill "The Mill Reach" when been(party, millyard) "A weir, a lock, a lever, and two men in grey coats who have not yet been told they are in a story.".
  Chapter ch_foot "Highfoot" when been(party, ferry_stage) "The last of the river. After this there is only the hill, and whatever you have chosen to carry up it.".

  Objective get_away when t0() > 0 and not boxReturned(party) and not caught(party) and not bessTook(party) "Get down the Aldwater and over the hills before a toll-clerk, or the Trust's two lads, catch you with something that is not yours.".
  Objective what_is_it when holding(party, music_box) and not drawerOpen(party) "There is a music box in the hamper. It plays a tune everyone on the river knows. It has a back-plate nobody has looked behind.".
  Objective hob_wait when hobMet(party) and not boxReturned(party) "Hob Garrod is in the Pelham lock-up, and has asked that Bess Lowther be told.".

  Milestone m_afloat "got away from Staithe on the wrong boat" worth 100 when been(party, deck).
  Milestone m_accused "was shouted at on a quay for a hamper" worth 60 when accused(party).
  Milestone m_fen "crossed the Wend Fen" worth 120 when been(party, bell_cot) or been(party, eel_stage).
  Milestone m_fair "went through Pelham on fair-day and was not caught" worth 150 when been(party, fairground) and been(party, millyard).
  Milestone m_lie "lied to a woman's face about a box" worth 120 when bessMet(party) and bessKnows(party).
  Milestone m_tune "heard the song the box was made for" worth 100 when knows(party, tune_known).
  Milestone m_plate "read what was scratched in the back-plate" worth 150 when knows(party, maker_known).
  Milestone m_hob "heard Hob Garrod out" worth 100 when hobMet(party).
  Milestone m_gap "got to the gap in the hills" worth 300 when been(party, pass_gap).
  Milestone m_swept "left two of the sergeant's men to the weir" worth 200 when ladsSwept(party).
  Milestone m_chain "crossed the Highfoot ferry chain hand over hand" worth 200 when chained(party) and not chainFell(party).

  // What the chances of the river leave behind.
  Observe galley_duty near teague when galleyDuty(party) and at(party, galley) "You have been peeling since Staithe. There is an onion in your hair, and Mrs Brabant has given up apologising for it.".
  Observe bess_pitied_note near bess when bessPitied(party) and bessMet(party) "Bess has stopped hurrying. She is still coming, but she is walking now.".
  Observe bess_hob_note near bess when hobKnown(party) and bessAlly(party) "Bess has asked three times how far to Pelham, and the third time she did not wait for the answer.".
  Observe shim_loyal_note near shim when shimLoyal(party) and travelsWith(shim, party) and at(party, weir) "Shim looks at the water and then, carefully, at nothing.".

  // Fiasco at the fair: the one thing nobody can see coming is a horse.
  Relation tradedDally(group).
  Action trade_to_dally(actor: group, site: place) "Trade the music box to Mr Dally for his horse, Parnassus" {
    Speaker dally.
    Requires able(actor) and company(actor) and at(actor, site) and at(actor, horse_lines) and travelsWith(dally, actor) and holding(actor, music_box) and dallyBolted(actor) and not tradedDally(actor).
    Time 0.
    On success { Spend music_box from actor. Assert tradedDally(actor). }
    Result "'For Hester,' says Mr Dally, taking it as a man takes a diploma. 'For when she asks why I was late, and why I came, and where I got a music box.' He gives you the reins of a long-faced bay with a look of grave surprise. 'He is a very fine horse,' he says. 'He does not like going forwards.'".
  }

  // ── Endings ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Ending beaten "Left on the Towpath" when dead(party) "The larger lad did not mean it. That is said afterwards, a good deal, in the Trust's room over the toll-house, and nobody is persuaded. The box goes back down the bank in a sack with the smaller one holding it, not looking at what is left, and the weir keeps on going over its apron, white and loud.".
  Ending chain_fell "The Aldwater Keeps It" when chainFell(party) "You are over, with your hands skinned and your pack light. On the stage behind you a woman has arrived at a run and stopped at the edge. She looks at the water for a long time. Then she sits down on the planks, with her back to you, and you cannot hear whether she is crying or counting.".
  Ending caught "Taken on the Towpath" when caught(party) "The larger lad has it under his arm, and the smaller has not looked at you once. You walk the rest of the way to Highfoot with your pack light and your hands empty. A little behind you a toll-clerk will come along the same bank, and find nobody, and a wet patch on the stone, and sit down on it.".
  Ending bess_took "Her Hands on the Box" when bessTook(party) "She has the box, and she has not hurt anyone, and it is the worst of all the things that could have happened. She carries it away from you in both hands, up the bank, and you do not follow, because there is nothing to follow for. Behind, it begins to play, and she walks faster.".
  Ending returned "The Lowther Kitchen" when boxReturned(party) "Bess Lowther carries it home in both hands, as if it might spill, and sets it on the table in the room over the toll-house. She does not wind it. She sits and looks at it until the light goes. You were not asked to stay, and you do not, but you hear it from the street, at the third winding, when she finally does. It plays the tune right through, and then there is a very small sound, like a latch.".
  Ending bargain "A Glorious Bad Bargain" when tradedDally(party) "You ride out of the horse lines on the long-faced bay, who goes sideways, and Mr Dally leaves on foot with a music box under his arm and every church bell in the county against him. At the third milestone the horse stops and looks at you with great intelligence. At the fourth it lies down. Three hours later a stout man with a gun and a pale girl with a dog pass in a wagon the other way, and Mr Dally is in the back of it holding the music box and saying, with enormous dignity, that he has never been so happy. The horse has got up.".
  Ending delivered "Forty Coin and a Back-plate" when soldQuill(party) "Barnaby Fosse winds it once as you leave, to see it work. It plays to the end. 'B.L., from T.L.,' he says to the shelf of stopped clocks. You are halfway to the gap with forty coin before you turn, and look back at the inn with the sign that has lost its picture, and wish you had read the plate first.".
  Ending hand_over_hand "Hand over Hand" when chained(party) and not chainFell(party) and at(party, far_bank) "You lie on the far stones with your hands burning and the box where it was. Across the river the stage is a small plank rectangle with two people on it, not shouting, and the ferry swinging empty on its chain. Una stands in her door with her arms folded. She does not look at you. She lifts one hand a little, as at a boy who has done a thing in the water that she once did herself.".
  Ending lost_friend "Without Shim" over the_weir when at(party, pass_gap) and shimGone(party) and holding(party, music_box) "The gap is windy and bare. You have the box and the road, and you do not have the boy who shouted the news of every barge on the river at nobody. At the crest you turn, once, and below at the Highfoot stage, small as a pin, there is a figure with its hand up. You wave. You cannot tell if he sees.".
  Ending with_bess "Bess at the Gap" over lost_friend when at(party, pass_gap) and bessAlly(party) and holding(party, music_box) "Bess Lowther stops at the crest with her coin-scale hanging forgotten in her hand and looks out at the hills as if they had been put there as a courtesy. 'I've never been this far,' she says. 'I'd supposed the river was all there was.' She holds out her hand, and you give her the box, and she does not wind it. 'Not till I've said it to him,' she says. She turns back down the hill alone, towards Pelham and a man in a lock-up. You stand on the crest with your hands empty and your faces cold.".
  Ending with_shim "Shim at the Gap" over clean when at(party, pass_gap) and shimGoesOn(party) and travelsWith(shim, party) and holding(party, music_box) "Shim comes up the last of the hill ahead of you, three yards at a time, and stands in the notch with his bundle and shouts the news of the sea at it. 'IT'S A VERY LARGE ONE!' he says. 'IT'S GOT NOTHING ON IT!' He is delighted. He has never been further than Pelham. The box in your pack is warm, from the sun, or from something.".
  Ending the_weir "Down the Weir" when at(party, pass_gap) and holding(party, music_box) and ladsSwept(party) "You come over the gap with the box and with two men in grey coats somewhere in the Aldwater below you, drying out. The sergeant will say he sent them for a lost dog. You wound the box once, on the river, and not since. It occurs to you at the top of the hill that you do not know the song, and that you have done a great deal to keep a thing you do not understand.".
  Ending cashed "Fifty Coin and No Questions" when at(party, pass_gap) and soldHonest(party) "You come over the gap with fifty coin, which is as much as most people get from a river. Behind, a horse-dealer winds a music box for his wife, and in a toll-house at Staithe a woman sits on her stool with three red lines in the ledger and a face like a closed door.".
  Ending empty "Empty Hands" when at(party, pass_gap) and dropped(party) "You cross the gap with nothing in your hands at all. It is a clear morning, and the hills go on. Somewhere under the Aldwater a box of dark wood is lying in the mud with its spring let go, and every so often, when the current moves it, it plays one note, and stops.".
  Ending hamper "Over the Gap with a Hamper" when at(party, pass_gap) and holding(party, hamper_kind) "You have carried it all the way up the hill, unopened, as you were told. At the crest you put it down and look at the label, DO NOT OPEN, in a hand that falls off its Ds like a roof. Nobody is behind you. You are still not sure whose it is. You sit on it, and eat a cake you do not have, and look at the sea.".
  Ending clean "Clean Water" when at(party, pass_gap) and holding(party, music_box) "The gap is a notch in the hills with the sea beyond, or a light that is not sky. You have the box and the road, and as far as you can see nobody behind you. You wind it, there on the crest, to see what all the fuss was, and it plays the whole tune, a man's tune, written in a hurry for a wife, and the wind takes it away down the other side.".
  Ending gap_any "Over the Gap" when at(party, pass_gap) "You come over the gap with nothing to show for the river but the river. It is quite enough to be going on with.".
}
